{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:21165295 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:21165295 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"21165295","source":"MED","pmid":"21165295","pmcid":"PMC2995234","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC2995234"]},"doi":"10.3346/jkms.2010.25.12.1784","title":"Effect of probiotic Lactobacillus (Lacidofil® cap) for the prevention of antibiotic-associated diarrhea: a prospective, randomized, double-blind, multicenter study.","authorString":"Song HJ, Kim JY, Jung SA, Kim SE, Park HS, Jeong Y, Hong SP, Cheon JH, Kim WH, Kim HJ, Ye BD, Yang SK, Kim SW, Shin SJ, Kim HS, Sung JK, Kim EY.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Song HJ","lastName":"Song","firstName":"Hyun Joo","initials":"HJ","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Internal Medicine and Preventive Medicine, Ewha Womans University School of Medicine, Seoul, Korea."}]}},{"fullName":"Kim JY","lastName":"Kim","firstName":"Jin-Yong","initials":"JY"},{"fullName":"Jung SA","lastName":"Jung","firstName":"Sung-Ae","initials":"SA"},{"fullName":"Kim SE","lastName":"Kim","firstName":"Seong-Eun","initials":"SE"},{"fullName":"Park HS","lastName":"Park","firstName":"Hye-Sook","initials":"HS","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9359-6522"}},{"fullName":"Jeong Y","lastName":"Jeong","firstName":"Yoolwon","initials":"Y","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8179-4620"}},{"fullName":"Hong SP","lastName":"Hong","firstName":"Sung Pil","initials":"SP"},{"fullName":"Cheon JH","lastName":"Cheon","firstName":"Jae Hee","initials":"JH","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2282-8904"}},{"fullName":"Kim WH","lastName":"Kim","firstName":"Won Ho","initials":"WH"},{"fullName":"Kim HJ","lastName":"Kim","firstName":"Hyo-Jong","initials":"HJ"},{"fullName":"Ye BD","lastName":"Ye","firstName":"Byong Duk","initials":"BD","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6647-6325"}},{"fullName":"Yang SK","lastName":"Yang","firstName":"Suk-Kyun","initials":"SK"},{"fullName":"Kim SW","lastName":"Kim","firstName":"Sang-Woo","initials":"SW"},{"fullName":"Shin SJ","lastName":"Shin","firstName":"Sung-Jae","initials":"SJ"},{"fullName":"Kim HS","lastName":"Kim","firstName":"Hyun-Soo","initials":"HS"},{"fullName":"Sung JK","lastName":"Sung","firstName":"Jae-Kyu","initials":"JK","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9068-624X"}},{"fullName":"Kim EY","lastName":"Kim","firstName":"Eun Young","initials":"EY"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-6647-6325"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8179-4620"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2282-8904"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-5682-9972"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6310-5366"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9068-624X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9359-6522"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2068-7287"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["recommended_reviews"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"12","volume":"25","journalIssueId":1792970,"dateOfPublication":"2010 Dec","monthOfPublication":12,"yearOfPublication":2010,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"J Korean Med Sci","title":"Journal of Korean medical science","essn":"1598-6357","issn":"1598-6357","isoabbreviation":"J Korean Med Sci","nlmid":"8703518"},"printPublicationDate":"2010-12-01"},"pubYear":"2010","pageInfo":"1784-1791","abstractText":"Antibiotic-associated diarrhea (AAD) is a common complication of antibiotic use. There is growing interest in probiotics for the treatment of AAD and Clostridium difficile infection because of the wide availability of probiotics. The aim of this multicenter, randomized, placebo-controlled, double-blind trial was to assess the efficacy of probiotic Lactobacillus (Lacidofil® cap) for the prevention of AAD in adults. From September 2008 to November 2009, a total of 214 patients with respiratory tract infection who had begun receiving antibiotics were randomized to receive Lactobacillus (Lacidofil® cap) or placebo for 14 days. Patients recorded bowel frequency and stool consistency daily for 14 days. The primary outcome was the proportion of patients who developed AAD within 14 days of enrollment. AAD developed in 4 (3.9%) of 103 patients in the Lactobacillus group and in 8 (7.2%) of 111 patients in the placebo group (P=0.44). However, the Lactobacillus group showed lower change in bowel frequency and consistency (50/103, 48.5%) than the placebo group (35/111, 31.5%) (P=0.01). Although the Lacidofil® cap does not reduce the rate of occurrence of AAD in adult patients with respiratory tract infection who have taken antibiotics, the Lactobacillus group maintains their bowel habits to a greater extent than the placebo group.","affiliation":"Department of Internal Medicine and Preventive Medicine, Ewha Womans University School of Medicine, Seoul, Korea.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Multicenter Study","Randomized Controlled Trial","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Lactobacillus"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Respiratory Tract Infections","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"DT","qualifierName":"drug therapy"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Diarrhea","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CI","qualifierName":"chemically induced"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PC","qualifierName":"prevention & control"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Anti-Bacterial Agents","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"AE","qualifierName":"adverse effects"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"TU","qualifierName":"therapeutic use"}]}},{"majorTop